lisa-design:
Replay: a record is "the same" as an earlier one of the event when its rule set, rule, fired, actions, rail verdicts and reason match (inputs and time ignored). Only rules with a new record are applied, so set/link/cancel of a rule that already acted is never redone over later state; dispatch/notify/effect of the newly acting rules keep evt/<event>/<rule>/<i> keys (provider markers and task ids dedupe them). Replay creates the work item when a rule now fires for an event that had none, and updates the event's processed mark to name it. The server checks the catalog first (503) and maps a missing event to 404. The CLI client setup is shared (cmd/factory/client.go), dispatch included.
